/-!
# Least sufficient bubbles in an open-ended top

* `SufficientBubbles`: when a least sufficient sub-presentation exists
  (monotone sufficiency and the deletion core; Horn-definable sufficiency and
  its Horn closure; disjunction as the obstruction; cost against inclusion).
* `IdealCompletion`: an open-ended growth as a point of the ideal completion
  of a thin category of finite profiles, with its universal property, compact
  elements, finite-stage factorization, and the condition for a strongest top.
* `RuleTables`: points of the completion of finite rule tables are arbitrary
  partial rule tables; derivations at the top live in finite stages; least
  sufficient bubbles of a top are finite.
* `CertificateBubbles`: the same in the category of validated certificate-GSLT
  definitions with strict rule-retaining arrows, with a two-route
  counterexample to least sufficient bubbles and to cost agreeing with
  inclusion.
* `ComputationBubbles`: computation preservation; syntax-directed typing gives
  Horn obligations and a least bubble, the Horn closure; typing by evaluation
  gives incomparable repairs whose meet loses preservation.
* `CarrierBubbles`: language-cutting bubbles of a GSLT; the reachable cone is
  the least carrier for the full reachability observer, a single observation
  can have none, and the least carrier of an unbounded computation can be
  infinite.
* `ClosureSystems`: seven equivalent presentations of a closure system (meets,
  closure operators, prefixed points, Horn implications, reflective
  sub-orders, monads, least members above seeds); every monotone operator on
  bubbles is the one-step operator of a Horn theory, finitary exactly when it
  preserves directed unions; closure operators are the monads on a poset;
  least fixed points are initial algebras.
* `ChaoticIteration`: every fair schedule of monotone rules computes the same
  least solution, with at most one effective step per generator; depth-first
  search in clause order is order-dependent and incomplete, and depth-first
  search with a depth bound is sound, complete and independent of clause
  order.
* `DisjunctiveBubbles`: the sufficiency upset always exists, has the same
  minimal bubbles as the request, is principal exactly when a least bubble
  exists, and is generated by an antichain; joins and meets of requests;
  selection policies range over exactly the minimal bubbles.
* `CarveOut`: the generic sufficiency fibration; the principal requests form a
  proper sub-fibration closed under conjunction but not disjunction,
  isomorphic to the arrow order of the bubbles, and generating every request
  by disjunction; observers.
* `OpenTopPresentations`: inductive and coinductive presentations of the
  least computation bubble; infinite cones with and without finite-state
  presentations.
* `PresentationLimits`: Horn and dual Horn under complement; closure access
  and the membership-query lower bound; monotone Horn queries; hypothetical
  goals; the Horn envelope and Horn lower bounds; detecting meet-closure; sound
  portfolios of strategies.
* `PrologContrasts`: two-valued supported models against three-valued
  evidence; absence at stages of an unclosed growth and declared closings;
  equations modulo a declared theory; two term models; two readings of a
  repeated variable.
-/
